{"step_index":229,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T15:21:43Z","thinking":"The user reports issues with rust and incorrect highlighting, suggesting a problem in how the YOLOv8 classification model identifies and localizes these features. Given the model's reliance on global average pooling for classification, the network might be broadly activating across the entire surface of the metal, due to shared color or texture characteristics. Examining the model's Grad-CAM on spatial features will help to confirm this hypothesis and understand the root cause.\n\n\nThe low spatial resolution of the feature map (7x7) makes precise localization of fine defects like scratches impossible; the signal diffuses. A classification model, not trained for bounding box regression, will produce inaccurate bounding boxes that decrease the explainability score, contradicting the project goals. The problem statement emphasizes localizing defects only when the data supports it, and prioritizing explainability.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"find_by_name","args":{"MaxDepth":3,"Pattern":"*","SearchDirectory":"D:\\acceleration","toolAction":"Checking dataset files","toolSummary":"Search D:\\acceleration for test images"}}]}
